  "name": "THROMBIN III",
  "code": "1584",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>The Anti-Thrombin III test serves for the rapid determination of the physiological activitity of Anti-Thrombin III, and permits the diagnosis of hereditary and acquired Anti-Thromobin III deficiency which carry and elevated risk of Thrombosis. Acquired Anti Thrombin III deficiencies requently occur as a consequence of consumption following loarge operations or disseminated intravascular coagulation (DIC) in sepsis, nephrosis, liver parenchymal damage(hepatits, durg, intoxication , alcoholism) and estrogen-containing contraceptives. The test enables early<br>detection of patients with an elevated risk of thromobosis.</p>",
